From eb824f04d9815c01b9c982da37ef3b0d2891c51d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mostlys4nny <mostlys4nny@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 17:51:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] updater: copy the rootfs to the name the unpacker
 actually reads

Switching the rootfs to gzip changed updater-unpack.sh to read
/data/sailfishos-rootfs.tar.gz but left the updater-script copying the archive
to /data/sailfishos-rootfs.tar.bz2, so the unpacker found nothing:

    tar: /data/sailfishos-rootfs.tar.gz: No such file or directory
    extraction produced no rootfs in /data/.stowaways/sailfishos

The extraction check added in the same change is what turned this into a clean
abort instead of a bricked phone -- the installer stopped before writing
hybris-boot.img, so the existing system stayed bootable. Without that check this
would have flashed a kernel over an empty rootfs, which is exactly the failure it
was written for.
---
 updater-script | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/updater-script b/updater-script
index 2084f81..2416e59 100644
--- a/updater-script
+++ b/updater-script
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@ ui_print("Device check succeeded, mounting filesystems ...");
 mount("ext4", "EMMC", "%DATA_PART%", "/data");
 
 ui_print("Copying filesystem archive ...");
-package_extract_file("%IMAGE_FILE%", "/data/sailfishos-rootfs.tar.bz2");
+package_extract_file("%IMAGE_FILE%", "/data/sailfishos-rootfs.tar.gz");
 ui_print("Copying installation script ...");
 package_extract_file("updater-unpack.sh", "/tmp/updater-unpack.sh");
 
